# These are executed on Linux. A CRLF checkout on Windows would ship \r into
# shebangs and systemd directives, which fails as an unreadable
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M". Force LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# The Windows client (devbox.ps1 / devbox.cmd) is LF too, deliberately: the
# repo's pre-commit `mixed-line-ending --fix=lf` hook normalizes everything to
# LF, so pinning those two to CRLF here would just fight the hook forever.
# PowerShell reads LF scripts fine.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=lf
*.cmd       text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
devbox-report text eol=lf
